From f2f2763bdb0c9c5ed93b9f436f955bf5ff53d028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:25:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06938/11362] [outer-loop] fix all 10 pre-existing test
 failures + 2 live-agent bugs found along the way

Addresses the 10 pre-existing test failures established as a baseline earlier
this session (confirmed pre-existing via an isolated git-worktree comparison,
unrelated to this session's HUD-masking work).

Root causes and fixes:

1. PHASE A1 (commit 0fad75f38) raised SUBMITTED_TARGET_LEVELS 1->3 and
   SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT 0.0->1e-12, but several tests still hardcoded the
   pre-A1 values instead of reading live SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG:
   - test_experiment_4524_stop_after_levelup.py: compare policy.explorer.target_levels
     against SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG["target_levels"] instead of exp4524's own
     historical STOP_AT_SCORED_TARGET_LEVELS constant (left untouched -- it's
     exp4524's own validated historical record, not a live-config mirror).
   - test_experiment_4500_value_weight_remeasure.py: compare against live
     SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG["value_weight"] dynamically.
   - experiment_4505_submitted_agent_scoreboard.py: this was a SOURCE-level bug,
     not just a test bug -- artifact_schema_errors hard-required value_weight==0.0,
     so exp4505.run() would raise ValueError on every future invocation. Fixed the
     verdict logic, schema validation, and main() CLI default to track live config
     instead of a frozen literal; updated REQ-ARC-FCP-4505 spec text accordingly.

2. test_experiment_4617_graduate_spatial_value_head_live.py asserted
   "LearnedVerifier.load" does not appear anywhere in arc_loop_solve.py. PHASE A3
   (commit df207c1da) legitimately reintroduced it as a narrow, gated,
   last-resort self-play-bootstrap fallback in _live_verifier_for_adapter
   (development_proxy scope, never the live scored path). Replaced the blanket
   absence check with an ordering check (spatial checkpoint path always tried
   first).

3. test_experiment_4585_integration_gate.py hardcoded assertions against
   mod.INTEGRATED_PACKAGE_RELATIVE_PATH, but SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG now points
   at exp4643's later submission package. Decoupled the schema-success test via
   a synthetic config override, and made the run-writes test compare dynamically
   against live SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG instead of exp4585's own path constant.

Two live-agent bugs found and fixed while chasing exp5587 crashes (not part of
the original 10, but directly blocking verification of the fixes above and
worth fixing on discovery per project self-healing practice):

4. E3AgentPolicy.next_move crashed with ValueError: not enough values to unpack
   on a degenerate/empty frame (grid.ndim == 1, e.g. a post-terminal sentinel
   frame) at TWO call sites: the transition-collection block and the tier-1
   explore-phase per-action tick. Root-fixed by hardening detect_cell/to_logical
   in arc_executable_world_model.py to fall back safely on non-2D grids, plus a
   defensive try/except around the transition-collection block.

5. E3AgentPolicy._world_model_candidates referenced os.environ without a local
   `import os` (NameError on every call). This method is unconditionally called
   from the core tier-3 world-model induction path, silently caught by
   _induce_and_plan's blanket except-Exception handler -- meaning tier-3
   induction escalation has been completely broken on the LIVE SCORED agent
   since commit 4f3a4f1ef (2026-06-28), ~2 weeks, across 10 subsequent commits
   to this file. Fixed with a local `import os`.

Also fixes a dormant, unrelated bug surfaced by touching exp5240 for the first
time in a while: its build_artifact hardcoded a non-standard
inference_substrate value ("arc_live_path_patch_synthesis") that was never
legal under CLAUDE.md's Inference-Substrate Declaration Discipline's fixed
enum, and never declared duration_s at all (masked because the invalid
substrate short-circuited the ARC artifact lint before the duration-floor
check could run). Corrected to aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts and added
real measured wall-clock duration_s; updated REQ-REPORT-5240 spec text.

With the two live-agent bugs fixed, exp5587 (does the HUD-mask levels_gained
win from exp5586's bare-config full-roster measurement transfer to the real
E3AgentPolicy cascade?) now runs cleanly to completion instead of crashing.
Result is an honest, self-flagged null: replicates_exp5586_pattern=False,
zero levels_gained delta across all 6 targeted games under the real cascade
config. adversarial_verify.py flags one expected FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK warning
(no headroom observed under either arm), consistent with CLAUDE.md discipline.

Verified: all 10 originally-failing tests pass individually; full 53-file
arc_competition_agent regression sweep (plus new test files) reaches 353
passed, 0 failed.

